{"excerpt_id":"ex_923564b918e1_009","source_id":"src_923564b918e1","source_hash":"88a5827f277779d003d3812e631d24e56d0c571d05113cb68c5f5ed7bdb3c756","text":"Abstract: We study a family of four-dimensional, asymptotically flat, charged black holes that develop (charged) scalar hair as one increases their charge at fixed mass. Surprisingly, the maximum charge for given mass is a nonsingular hairy black hole with nonzero Hawking temperature. The implications for Hawking evaporation are discussed.","location_hint":"paragraph 24","char_start":1187,"char_end":1528,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T21:17:42.582Z"}
